Parity with the upstream, verified
----------------------------------

158 upstream files were compared against this port with link targets stripped
(paths moved; rules must not). Result: **157 identical on rule text, 0 missing,
0 added, 1 differing** — `references/imagery-kit.md`, which carries one added
provenance paragraph (delta 9 below). The flow's ten steps (0, 1, 2, 2.5, 2.6,
3, 4, 5, 6, 7), all 21 macrostructures, all 20 themes, all 50 component
archetypes, all 4 genres, the 6 cross-verb disciplines, the 3 verbs, the
component-scope branch, and the 58-gate slop test are present unchanged.


What this port changes, exhaustively
------------------------------------

Surface identity

 1. Renamed to the Asgard engine identity throughout. The output stamp is
    `/* Freyja4 · ... */` and the verbs are `freyja4 audit|redesign|study`.
 2. The Step 5 preview block's version string reads `Freyja4 · v1.0.0`, matching
    this plugin's version rather than the upstream skill's.
 3. Removed upstream sponsor branding from prompt copy. Third-party companies
    named inside theme notes as *design references* are kept — those are factual
    citations, not branding.

Relocations (paths moved; no rule text altered)

 4. Project memory moved from a project-root dotfile to the Freyja vault at
    `.asgard/.vanadis/engine4/` (log.json, preflight.json), matching engines 1,
    2 and 3. Upstream's "respect any existing .gitignore" line becomes "the
    vault is already outside git — never add an ignore entry", which is the
    Asgard vault rule.
 5. Vendored, because the skill's own rules read them and the upstream shipped
    them outside the skill directory:
      references/tokens.css      ← site/css/tokens.css (the theme-diversification
                                   rule reads its per-theme axis comments)
      references/examples/       ← site/_tests/ minus _thumbs (worked builds cited
                                   by hero-enrichment.md and by the human docs)
      references/human/          ← docs/recipes.md, docs/study-examples.md (the
                                   two files SKILL.md marks "do NOT auto-load")
    Relative links were repointed to the new locations. Nothing else moved.

Additions (this port has rules the upstream does not)

 6. An `## Asgard contract` section ahead of the flow, carrying five clauses:
    the vault; "self-scoring is not a review"; delivery gates that must be
    reported by name with silence counted as unverified; numbers must name their
    source; Asgard-wide invariants are unchanged.
 7. `engine/scripts/slop_gate.mjs`, a dependency-free deterministic gate runtime
    the upstream did not have. Step 7 splits into 7a self-report (unchanged
    58-gate sweep), 7b machine verdict, 7c delivery gates. The Step 5 preview's
    "Slop test" row now carries both judgments, labelled apart.
 8. One added bullet in Step 6's Build list: no dead motion — a declared
    transition on a property nothing changes is a still image. This matches the
    `inert-transition` rule engines 2 and 3 already enforce.
 9. A host-provenance paragraph in `references/imagery-kit.md`: the imagery CDN
    is the upstream's host, not ours, so it is annotated as a may-vanish
    dependency rather than rewritten into a URL that would never resolve.
10. A header table naming engines 1–4 and their lanes, plus a rule that a
    composed build must say which engine owned which decision, and a paragraph
    in Step 4 handing real-object geometry to engine 3 instead of drawing it in
    CSS.

Deliberately NOT changed

11. `site/_tests/verbs/redesign/notes.md` links to `../refine/`, which does not
    exist upstream either. The port leaves the broken link alone and records it
    by name in `tests/test_freyja4.py`, so new breakage is still caught.


Two inconsistencies found inside the upstream corpus
----------------------------------------------------

Reported, not silently patched. Both are in the upstream's own files.

  A. `tokens.css` defines `--color-accent-ink` as the accent tuned for use AS
     text — in the Studio theme it is byte-identical to `--color-accent`. Slop
     test gate 41 reads the same token as the ink placed ON an accent fill.
     Following gate 41 literally against the shipped token yields red on red.
     `slop_gate.mjs` therefore judges the substance (is text on an accent fill
     readable) and reports the missing name as a note rather than a failure.

  B. The Brutal theme ships neutrals at chroma 0.001–0.003, while gate 22 in the
     same corpus requires a 0.005 floor. The shipped theme violates its own
     gate. Builds using Brutal must lift the neutrals and say so.
